{"AuthzClientCryptoProvider is registered as a full CryptoProvider SPI implementation but only implements ECDSA/keystore methods, throwing UnsupportedOperationException for most SPI methods, which will cause runtime failures when selected outside the narrow ECDSA-conversion use case": 0.8301742076873779, "AuthzClient.create() unconditionally calls CryptoIntegration.init() which mutates the process-wide crypto singleton based on authz-client classloader, causing a module-boundary leak that can interfere with applications that already initialized crypto differently": 0.6138204336166382, "ASN1Decoder.readSequence() does not properly handle indefinite-length encodings - when readLength() returns -1, the while loop is skipped and returns an empty sequence instead of rejecting unsupported input": 0.8978087902069092, "ASN1Decoder implementation never checks for zero-progress or indefinite nested lengths, allowing malformed ASN.1 streams to be misparsed or cause incorrect behavior instead of failing fast": 0.686158299446106, "ASN1Decoder.readLength() incorrectly rejects valid payloads whose encoded length equals the buffer size by throwing 'corrupted stream' when length >= limit, even though this is valid DER": 0.51749587059021, "CryptoIntegration provider-selection behavior changed from failing on multiple providers to sorting by order() and selecting highest-ranked, but documentation still implies exactly one provider is required": 0.25408706068992615, "dumpSecurityProperties() logs sensitive security configuration including truststore/keystore paths and security-provider configuration when trace logging is enabled, which can leak sensitive operational information": 0.0755673348903656, "CryptoProvider.order() Javadoc is incomplete about tie/fallback semantics - does not document that selection is deterministic by sorting and that equal-order providers depend on loader iteration order": 0.06313743442296982}